WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.369
-She was the EPA...
-MONA: Something cheerful.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.003
(LAUGHS) ...administrator
under President Obama

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:07.339
who is now the director
of Harvard Center for Health
and the Global Environment,

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.042
my old job, Gina McCarthy!

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.544
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)
-BILL: Hey.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.749
-Gina, how are you?
-GINA: Good to see you.

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:17.850
BILL: I...

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.720
-always love having you on.
-Thank you.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:21.988
Because you're
a straight-shooter,

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.423
and you are so missed
in your old job.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.994
-I know. Don't I look good, now?
-And I... You look good now.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.129
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:33.199
And I love the way you stick up
for the agency,

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.835
and I love the way
you always put it in context.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.536
You know, I read something
recently where you said,

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.939
"You know, the EPA,
it's not about polar bears."

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.641
-No.
-And I'm in love
with polar bears.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.042
I think we should
save every one.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.678
But people just don't,
I think, understand.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:49.916
They've somehow got this idea
that the EPA is not for them,
that it's working against them.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.785
-How did that--
-Just because it has the word
"environment" in it,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.588
it doesn't mean we do
birds and bunnies
and polar bears.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.556
-(LAUGHS) Right.
-You know?
Although, I love them,

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.492
-so don't send me
bad emails about it.
-Right.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.994
It's really about kids.
It's about public health.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:05.765
-It's about safe drinking water,
clean land. It's clean air.
-Right. It's-- Yeah.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.400
-What is that?
-Yeah.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.036
(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.139
-And the man who took over,
Scot Pruitt...
-Yes.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.275
-That's not what he's about.
-That's not what he is about.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:18.844
How bad is it
under Scott Pruitt?

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:20.980
It couldn't be worse,
right? He...

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.616
It's true. The only thing
that could be worse

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.851
is if he actually knew
what he was doing.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.020
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.122
-But I think he--
-It's true.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.657
I think he does know
what he's doing.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:31.958
He knows how
to dismantle something.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:34.827
Yeah, well, he's got an all-out
attack on science, for sure.

00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:37.263
He's got an all-out attack
on the agency.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.133
You know, he's making some
policy decisions,

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:43.069
but in the end, he's trying
to get rid of a lot of rules

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.471
that were put in place
that were done well,

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.507
and every time there have been
challenges in court,
he's going down.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:49.842
BILL: And you know, I hate to--

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:53.780
(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.282
I hate to drag religion
into things...

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.484
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:58.584 --> 00:01:59.885
...but it is a lot--

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:03.656
I'm sorry, but a lot of these
anti-environmental people

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:08.261
are that way because they are
religious, excuse me, nuts...

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:13.566
who believe Jesus is going
to take the wheel, and-- and...

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.534
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:15.768
-Right?
-Great song.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.203
Great song,
but terrible policy...

00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:20.172
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-Uh...

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.174
and that we don't have to do
anything, because,

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:26.179
as this fellow guy from
Oklahoma says, Inhofe,

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:27.479
"God's still up there."

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:28.681
-I know.
-You know?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.850
"What do we need you for, Gina,
God's still up there.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.018
Case closed."

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.654
Well, that is one way
to look at it.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.857
EPA tends to look at science,

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.492 line:0%
because science isn't
a religion, it's facts.

00:02:40.592 --> 00:02:41.660 line:0%
There ya go. Okay, so...

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.097 line:0%
And we really like to make
decisions like that, so...

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:47.266 line:0%
-So here's...
-(APPLAUSE)

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.201
Here's my problem
with regulation,

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:50.903
and I know we need a lot
of regulation

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.773
and I think we probably need
almost all the EPA regulation,

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:57.509
but we have a lot of regulation
that is really onerous.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.545
-Even Obama used to say that.
-Hmm.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.914
And it gives the whole thing
a bad name,

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:03.983
which brings me to my
garage door.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.284
(GINA LAUGHS)

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.620
-I knew something was coming.
-I just-- Yeah.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.688
I just wanted to get a new
garage door.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:11.857
You know what you have to do
in California

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:12.926
to get a new garage--

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.426
And it's my garage door,
by the way.

00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:17.530
If I want it to fall on my face,
I should be allowed.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.298
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.967
Maybe I want to commit suicide
by garage door.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:22.935
(GINA LAUGHS)

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:26.005
I mean, you need-- Like, I had
three or four inspections.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:29.141
It took months and months
to put in a goddamn garage door.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:32.178
I'm not askin' for a helipad
over my house.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.681
And things like that give
regulation a bad name,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.516
and thats-- and it hurts
the EPA.

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:39.852
I just wanted to share that
about my garage door.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.421
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.390
(APPLAUSE)

00:03:46.124 --> 00:03:47.760
You don't have to answer that!

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:49.695
-I'm glad we settled that!
-Yes, okay...

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:52.732
So, here's something else, I,
you know, I...

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.100
we're probably around
the same generation.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.203
-Yes. Generally, yes.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:03:58.303 --> 00:04:01.874
Okay. So, I read the obituaries.
I always have, by the way.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.342
I always thought
they were very amusing.

00:04:03.408 --> 00:04:04.410
Now, they're not so amusing.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.712
-They're more relevant than
they used to be, aren't they?
-Oh, my God.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.147
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.615
"Ninety-three... young man"

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.318
-(GINA LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.753
What, was he hit by a bus?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.289
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:20.426
But... But, you know...
I just see the word "cancer."

00:04:20.492 --> 00:04:21.660
Yeah.

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:23.262
I mean, every day. All the time.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.064
And I remember in the '80s,
when people were dying
from AIDS,

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:29.368
they didn't know how
to deal with it,
and people were like,

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:34.172
"I see the name of this disease
every week in the paper,
we've got to do something."

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:39.244
But I see this word "cancer"
all the time.
I know we've always had it,

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.447
although, it was rare
in the ancient world.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.482
We've had it more
as we go along.

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:47.152
Now it seems that we have--
It's just in every obituary,

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.389
and... it's because of
the environment.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:53.493
It's the lead, it's the mercury,
it's the water, it's the food,
it's the oceans.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:54.493
Yeah.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.497
What don't people get?
I guess they just think
it's gonna be the next guy.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.634
Well, I think what happened is,
because we are from
the same generation,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.605 line:0%
we remember when rivers
were burning and smoke stacks
were spewing out smoke.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:06.906 line:0%
Right.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.740 line:0%
It's just it's not
as visible anymore,

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.776 line:0%
but it doesn't mean
it has gone away,

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.478 line:0%
it means it is way more
insidious than it used to be.

00:05:13.745 --> 00:05:17.049
I don't think I need to say
more than "Flint, Michigan,"
to remind people--

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.183
-BILL: Right.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.518
...that kids
are getting contaminated.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:23.489
You know, and I...
We just have to--

00:05:23.555 --> 00:05:29.128
Scientists have to speak
very clearly, and we have to
let scientists tell the truth.

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:32.731
-And we have to listen to it
and base decisions on it.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:37.269
You know, I...
One of my favorite things
to say when I go out is,

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.905
"Listen, this is all you
really need to know
about climate change:

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:44.443
Number one, it's real.
Number two, man-made emissions
caused it.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.279
And number three,
that's why women
need to rule the world."

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:50.316
-(CHEERING)
-It's as simple as that.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.952
-(LAUGHS)
-(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.488
(CHEERING CONTINUES)

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.858
-BILL: Okay.
-I'm sick of cleaning up
after you guys.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:05:59.959
-BILL: No, I...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

